  "subject": "🤖 AI Agents Daily — Banks Are Blocking AI Agents—and Handing Customers the Bill | November 22, 2026",
  "htmlBody": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\">\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <meta name=\"x-apple-disable-message-reformatting\" />\n  <!--[if !mso]><!-->\n  <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge\" />\n  <!--<![endif]-->\n  <title>🤖 AI Agents Daily — Banks Are Blocking AI Agents—and Handing Customers the Bill | November 22, 2026</title>\n</head>\n<body style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#f0f0f0;-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%;-ms-text-size-adjust:100%;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\">\n\n<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ OUTER WRAPPER -->\n<table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#f0f0f0\"\n       style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:24px 10px;\">\n\n      <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>\n      <table width=\"680\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"center\"><tr><td>\n      <![endif]-->\n\n      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ MAIN CONTAINER -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#ffffff\"\n             style=\"max-width:680px;border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;box-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.10);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;\">\n\n        <!-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── HEADER -->\n        <tr>\n          <td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#ffffff\"\n              style=\"padding:40px 30px 28px 30px;border-bottom:2px solid #009c6d;\">\n\n            <!-- Logo emoji -->\n            <div style=\"font-size:40px;line-height:1;margin-bottom:12px;\">🤖</div>\n\n            <!-- Publication title -->\n            <h1 style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;\n                        font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;letter-spacing:-0.5px;\n                        line-height:1.2;\">\n              AI Agents Daily\n            </h1>\n\n            <!-- Tagline -->\n            <p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;font-size:14px;color:#666666;\n                      font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.5;\">\n              AI developments that matter for financial institutions\n            </p>\n\n            <!-- Date -->\n            <p style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#999999;\n                      font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">\n              November 22, 2026\n            </p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- ──────────────────────────────────────── DEEP DIVE SECTION -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:40px 30px 0 30px;\">\n\n            <!-- Section header -->\n            <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 22px 0;font-size:22px;font-weight:bold;color:#009c6d;\n                        font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.3;\">\n              Deep Dive 🔍\n            </h2>\n\n            <!-- Deep dive article title -->\n            <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 18px 0;font-size:21px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;\n                        font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;line-height:1.4;\">\n              Banks Are Blocking AI Agents—and Handing Customers the Bill\n            </h3>\n\n            <!-- Deep dive article body (HTML from Claude, inline-styled by email-builder) -->\n            <div style=\"font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.75;\n                        font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\">\n              <h3 style=\"margin:24px 0 10px 0;font-size:12px;font-weight:bold;color:#009c6d;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-bottom:8px;\">Overview</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.75;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\"><strong>Major US banks are slamming the door on third-party AI agents</strong>—and when automated bots make unauthorized moves on customer accounts, the message from Wells Fargo, Citi, and others is clear: that's on you. <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMic0FVX3lxTE9pUy1ObG9vc0x4SEwtc2xRdFNzNldlekRzdXZhOTNWZnByOUh2TzRsUEI2dWhiM2Y3cmZEZGZrQ1RBLUx5VDhreGo5YW1GRVZtZnNlNmlRSjFvRlFkcnlwZFEtYnJFOUZ3SWxrYlZfWG5ka3c\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:none;\">WIRED reports</a> the industry has collectively decided to shift liability to customers before regulators establish any standard.</p><h3 style=\"margin:24px 0 10px 0;font-size:12px;font-weight:bold;color:#009c6d;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-bottom:8px;\">The Details</h3><ul style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;padding:0 0 0 20px;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.75;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Wells Fargo has explicitly told customers that third-party AI agents operate \"at your own risk\"—zero bank liability</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Citi has stated customers bear personal responsibility when AI banking agents \"go rogue\" and cause account harm</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Wall Street banks broadly are demanding guardrails for rogue AI agents, per Bloomberg</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Canadian big banks are closing the door on AI tools that hold customer banking credentials</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">59% of financial institutions have already deployed AI agents, yet only 5% have reached operational maturity</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Singapore's MAS is taking the opposite approach: announcing a formal \"Know Your Agent\" protocol and an agentic money sandbox for supervised testing</li></ul><h3 style=\"margin:24px 0 10px 0;font-size:12px;font-weight:bold;color:#009c6d;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-bottom:8px;\">Why It Matters</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.75;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\">Banks choosing \"at your own risk\" disclaimers over governance frameworks are setting a troubling precedent. Customers expect AI-powered convenience, and blanket liability waivers won't survive regulatory scrutiny in the EU, UK, or soon the US. Institutions offloading accountability now may face harder reckoning once consumer protection rules catch up with the technology.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.75;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\">For fintechs and neobanks, this is a structural opening. If incumbents refuse to accommodate AI agents, API-first and AI-native players gain a real competitive edge. Singapore's MAS sandbox hints at where smart regulation heads: not a ban, but a formal Know Your Agent (KYA) framework requiring banks to authenticate and audit every agent acting on a customer's behalf.</p>\n            </div>\n\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- ─────────────────────────────── DIVIDER: Deep Dive → Things to Know -->\n        <tr>\n          <td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:36px 0;\">\n            <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>\n            <table width=\"340\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"center\"><tr>\n            <td height=\"3\" bgcolor=\"#009c6d\" style=\"font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</td>\n            </tr></table>\n            <![endif]-->\n            <!--[if !mso]><!-->\n            <div style=\"width:50%;height:3px;background-color:#009c6d;margin:0 auto;\"></div>\n            <!--<![endif]-->\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- ─────────────────────────────── THINGS TO KNOW SECTION -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 30px 0 30px;\">\n\n            <!-- Section header -->\n            <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 22px 0;font-size:22px;font-weight:bold;color:#009c6d;\n                        font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.3;\">\n              Things to Know 👀\n            </h2>\n\n            <!-- Things to Know entries injected by email-builder -->\n            \n      <!-- TTK entry 1 -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"\n             style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 4px 0;font-size:16px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;\">\n            1. <strong>MAS Outlines 'Know Your Agent' Protocol and Agentic Money Sandbox, Warns Against Sharing Financial Logins with AI Agents</strong>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Source (linked) -->\n        \n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 8px 0;font-size:12px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#009c6d;\">\n            <a href=\"https://news.google.\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:underline;\">Hubbis</a>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Summary -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 10px 0;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.7;\">\n            Singapore's MAS has outlined a formal Know Your Agent (KYA) framework requiring financial institutions to identify and authenticate AI agents acting on customer accounts. MAS also launched an Agentic Money Sandbox for supervised testing of AI-enabled transactions, and explicitly warned against sharing financial login credentials with AI agents.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Key point callout -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:8px 14px;font-size:14px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.6;background-color:#f8f8f8;\n                     border-left:3px solid #009c6d;margin-bottom:6px;\">\n            🧠 <strong>Regulatory first-mover.</strong> Singapore is establishing the first formal KYA compliance standard for AI agents in finance, giving banks a playbook while the US and EU are still deliberating on AI agent accountability frameworks.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr><td style=\"padding-bottom:6px;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Rule between entries -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:16px 0 20px 0;\">\n            <div style=\"height:1px;background-color:#e5e5e5;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n\n      <!-- TTK entry 2 -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"\n             style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 4px 0;font-size:16px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;\">\n            2. <strong>Only 5% of insurers and banks achieve AI agents maturity despite 59% adoption</strong>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Source (linked) -->\n        \n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 8px 0;font-size:12px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#009c6d;\">\n            <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifEFVX3lxTFBiYzQ3SkZNLVdLSWcwMkxsOGxhSjZGMmtKNEZSZjFtd1lPVXNRWWkwQ0JQNkFKMGxVWURtQ25TT0owNnk4WXFFdGtBTG04Q2ptUDdCZzQzcXd3OE9hd1ZZTi1PQzJQR0NhbHNSYnppeEk4MzRreTRUd2Frd3A\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:underline;\">Beinsure</a>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Summary -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 10px 0;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.7;\">\n            Despite 59% of insurers and banks having deployed AI agents, only 5% have achieved full operational maturity, per new Beinsure survey data. The gap reflects widespread shallow deployment—pilots and proofs-of-concept without the governance, risk management, or outcome-measurement frameworks needed to run agents at scale.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Key point callout -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:8px 14px;font-size:14px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.6;background-color:#f8f8f8;\n                     border-left:3px solid #009c6d;margin-bottom:6px;\">\n            🧠 <strong>Deployment without governance.</strong> Most financial institutions running AI agents today lack the oversight structures to manage liability or measure outcomes—making the accountability reckoning now erupting at Wells Fargo and Citi entirely predictable.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr><td style=\"padding-bottom:6px;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Rule between entries -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:16px 0 20px 0;\">\n            <div style=\"height:1px;background-color:#e5e5e5;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n\n      <!-- TTK entry 3 -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"\n             style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 4px 0;font-size:16px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;\">\n            3. <strong>Your AI agent has a wallet. Who answers for its decisions?</strong>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Source (linked) -->\n        \n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 8px 0;font-size:12px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#009c6d;\">\n            <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxPQ3lxNkNMbFM1Q3ZQbTJJYkpkcWFaX3dyWGFlSVNYeUlWZzFQdjhfaEh1N1lMVWRoVVBydmM4NU41NXgxLWFBZGxELU10WWsxa1YtdHJsZHl1LWZMb3RlYlNUbVdPWVc1WkFxMklNNDh2S2hRY050Y2RrdjF2YkNxYmhKc2Q4MWV3WVhhRw\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:underline;\">Fortune</a>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Summary -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 10px 0;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.7;\">\n            AI agents are increasingly granted digital wallets and financial account access to act autonomously—spending money, booking services, and executing decisions without direct human approval. Fortune's analysis highlights a growing accountability vacuum: when an AI agent's autonomous financial decision causes harm, liability attribution between user, platform, and institution remains legally undefined.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Key point callout -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:8px 14px;font-size:14px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.6;background-color:#f8f8f8;\n                     border-left:3px solid #009c6d;margin-bottom:6px;\">\n            🧠 <strong>Accountability vacuum.</strong> As AI agents gain spending authority, financial institutions need frameworks to identify, audit, and reverse agent-initiated transactions—or they risk both operational losses and regulatory censure when agents act outside user intent.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr><td style=\"padding-bottom:6px;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Rule between entries -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:16px 0 20px 0;\">\n            <div style=\"height:1px;background-color:#e5e5e5;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n\n      <!-- TTK entry 4 -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"\n             style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 4px 0;font-size:16px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;\">\n            4. <strong>Anthropic mathematician claims to have proved Riemann hypothesis with help of Claude</strong>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Source (linked) -->\n        \n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 8px 0;font-size:12px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#009c6d;\">\n            <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikgFBVV95cUxNTnliTkVvRWFBQ3NScjZ6bUlDT1plNFM3d3hDcWFsLVF2dnhnQW05QWZEc2tuaU5Ha2Y1b3g1bFdlSUd1eXF2b2VvT3hrNHN2dTJrRmZhN2QyWkhtY053UTlZN3dfQlpkMVBEclkxU0ZnMDFZanI4YTRWQ1F2YXhBd2Z3RVR5MXptR0poX3hYN0lMUQ\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:underline;\">The Independent</a>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Summary -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 10px 0;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.7;\">\n            An Anthropic mathematician has claimed a Claude-assisted proof of the Riemann hypothesis, one of the seven Millennium Prize Problems. Separately, Anthropic's Levent Alpöge and NYU's Tristan Buckmaster published a Claude-aided proof that Navier-Stokes equations can produce finite-time blow-up. Both proofs are undergoing community verification.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Key point callout -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:8px 14px;font-size:14px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.6;background-color:#f8f8f8;\n                     border-left:3px solid #009c6d;margin-bottom:6px;\">\n            🧠 <strong>AI as a mathematical reasoner.</strong> If verified, these results establish AI as a tool for high-stakes mathematical research—with downstream implications for cryptography, risk modeling, and the mathematics underpinning modern financial infrastructure.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr><td style=\"padding-bottom:6px;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Rule between entries -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:16px 0 20px 0;\">\n            <div style=\"height:1px;background-color:#e5e5e5;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n\n      <!-- TTK entry 5 -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"\n             style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 4px 0;font-size:16px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;\">\n            5. <strong>Anthropic (ANT) Puts Claude Into Enterprise Security As Its AI Builds Successors</strong>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Source (linked) -->\n        \n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 8px 0;font-size:12px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#009c6d;\">\n            <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiogFBVV95cUxNcG00NjY3R0Z5aTZDYkNMa2R3Q1F0blZvSHN5N1lGckwxa0R3LWdjc3ZIMFphcUxDdC1rWUVpVVNfN2VvOWJ3V09ELUNQQms1SzBBRWM2R0wxRGpFejc2b2k5MGNvb1lYT0xOcFE5S3ZiN0dFdEpSQkswWjlnMnZyU1BCQ095NG53U3RHMkJDZFowU28tcW9aS3RSMUcyeVlVc0E\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:underline;\">Yahoo Finance</a>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Summary -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 10px 0;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.7;\">\n            Anthropic went public at a $119.5B valuation, with South Korean retail investors purchasing approximately $164M of shares on IPO day. Concurrently, Anthropic is expanding Claude into enterprise security applications, moving toward infrastructure positioning beyond model-as-a-service.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Key point callout -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:8px 14px;font-size:14px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.6;background-color:#f8f8f8;\n                     border-left:3px solid #009c6d;margin-bottom:6px;\">\n            🧠 <strong>From vendor to infrastructure.</strong> Anthropic's enterprise security expansion post-IPO signals ambition to become foundational technology for large institutions—financial firms already deploying Claude should anticipate new offerings in risk, compliance, and security tooling.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr><td style=\"padding-bottom:6px;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Rule between entries -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:16px 0 20px 0;\">\n            <div style=\"height:1px;background-color:#e5e5e5;font-size:0;line-height:0;\">&nbsp;</div>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n\n      <!-- TTK entry 6 -->\n      <table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"\n             style=\"border-collapse:collapse;mso-table-lspace:0pt;mso-table-rspace:0pt;\">\n\n        <!-- Headline -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 4px 0;font-size:16px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;\">\n            6. <strong>Gemini 5 teased. Why Developers Think Google Has Already Achieved Recursive Self-Improvement?</strong>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Source (linked) -->\n        \n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 8px 0;font-size:12px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\n                     color:#009c6d;\">\n            <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxQQjNSaWc1NE1Nam95LWZnR1dRMHphVGs3bHJ6YUU5QV9Ia3FBUVJVcnMtbF9sSjZLRjNkZG1SZTkwLWJsc2VRXzAzOEduU1NVc09MT2ZEZmFaUDhPbzZRbVZCODNoN2ZlbEFDQlJ6MnRER0M4eUVhdURlMFNPNS1Kd2ZXcEpDbTFQZEdHREZ2R3JaMlcwN3c\" style=\"color:#009c6d;text-decoration:underline;\">Nokiapoweruser</a>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- Summary -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:0 0 10px 0;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.7;\">\n            Google teased Gemini 5 with developer speculation that recursive self-improvement techniques may be involved in model training. No formal benchmarks or release date have been given; the conversation has been driven by developer analysis of Gemini 4's training methodology and unexplained capability jumps.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        \n        <!-- Key point callout -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding:8px 14px;font-size:14px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;\n                     color:#333333;line-height:1.6;background-color:#f8f8f8;\n                     border-left:3px solid #009c6d;margin-bottom:6px;\">\n            🧠 <strong>Accelerating capability curve.</strong> If frontier models are meaningfully improving their own training pipelines, the pace of AI advancement will keep compressing—financial institutions should assume planning horizons for AI strategy will keep shortening.\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr><td style=\"padding-bottom:6px;font-